From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alan Bradburne <abradburne@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:20:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] mfd: rk8xx: route the sleep pin only while suspended

On the RG DS+ the RK817's SLEEP pin follows the SoC's PMU sleep output
(GPIO0_A2) once that pin is muxed to it, which deep sleep needs: without
it the PMIC never enters its sleep state and the regulators'
regulator-state-mem settings do nothing. Muxed there all the time (in the
"default" pinctrl state), a power-off leaves the PMIC so that the power
key no longer starts the device; only a long press, which resets the
PMIC, brings it back. Reproduced twice with nibOS's power-off after a
deep sleep; the same power-off with the pin left unmuxed starts again
from a short press.

Select a "sleep" pinctrl state in rk8xx_suspend() and go back to
"default" in rk8xx_resume() and before shutdown, as the vendor kernel's
pmic-sleep and pmic-power-off states do. Boards without a "sleep" state
are unaffected (pinctrl_pm_select_sleep_state() does nothing).

Upstream status: candidate.
---
 drivers/mfd/rk8xx-core.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/rk8xx-core.c b/drivers/mfd/rk8xx-core.c
--- a/drivers/mfd/rk8xx-core.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/rk8xx-core.c
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 #include <linux/mfd/rk808.h>
 #include <linux/mfd/core.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/pinctrl/consumer.h>
 #include <linux/property.h>
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
 #include <linux/reboot.h>
@@ -738,6 +739,13 @@
 	struct rk808 *rk808 = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Take the SoC's sleep output off the SLEEP pin before powering off:
+	 * routed there at power-off, the RK817 is left in a state the power
+	 * key can't start it from, and only a long press resets it.
+	 */
+	pinctrl_pm_select_default_state(dev);
+
 	switch (rk808->variant) {
 	case RK805_ID:
 		ret = regmap_update_bits(rk808->regmap,
@@ -929,6 +937,15 @@
 		break;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Route the SoC's sleep output to the SLEEP pin (the "sleep" pinctrl
+	 * state) only while suspended, as the vendor kernel does, so the
+	 * PMIC's sleep function and regulator-state-mem settings apply in deep
+	 * sleep without the pin staying routed through a power-off.
+	 */
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = pinctrl_pm_select_sleep_state(dev);
+
 	return ret;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(rk8xx_suspend);
@@ -938,6 +955,8 @@
 	struct rk808 *rk808 = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	int ret = 0;
 
+	pinctrl_pm_select_default_state(dev);
+
 	switch (rk808->variant) {
 	case RK809_ID:
 	case RK817_ID:
